[Music]  my parents  are jeannie bavaro and villa costa my  mom  is a producer director personal manager  still here in town my dad is a singer  impressionist  my parents had a show called lasting  impressions it was at the luxor  and then it was at the flamingo this was  actually  the finale costume in lasting  impressions and so all the  showgirls used to wear this and i was a  kid and i was backstage and i'd say  hello to them and now  all this time has passed and legends  kindly bought  these beautiful costumes and revamped  them and made them look  awesome for the show that we're in now  and i  am now here in legends in concert and i  get to wear them and it's  truly full circle to be able to now come  back  and wear something that was not only a  part of las vegas history but a part of  my own personal history and my family's  story is  it's really cool i really am proud to be  a part of this show  it's one of the few that brings back the  classic era of the showgirl  and glamour and just taste  in a show we dance our butts off  um we get to wear these gorgeous  costumes and it's just a lot of stuff  that i feel like is not commonplace  anymore  you know you see these huge productions  you have all these residencies and  they're great  they're wonderful but there is something  to be said for  just taking it back and going a little  bit more old school  and just remembering the classics and  what built this city and what makes  vegas vegas

